1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,580
Do you consider yourself wealthy?
你觉得自己富有吗？

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:06,260
Do you have enough cash in the bank to have no financial worries?
你是否有足够的现金，没有经济上的担忧？

3
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:10,040
Or maybe, like me, being rich is just something you can only dream about?
或者，也许像我一样，富有仅仅是你只能梦想的事情？

4
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:21,300
For most of us, the most likely way to become a millionaire is to win the lottery, but without buying a ticket, what other ways are there to get super- rich?
对大多数人来说，最可能成为百万富翁的机会是中彩票，但如果不买彩票，还有其他办法成为超级富豪吗？

5
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:31,900
A ‘super-rich‘ person is often defined as someone with over $30 million dollars of assets - so it’s not just about having a suitcase stuffed full of banknotes!
“超级富豪”通常指资产超过3000万美元的人——所以这不仅仅是拥有一只装满钞票的行李箱那么简单！

6
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:36,820
They usually own property, an expensive yacht or eat in swanky restaurants.
他们通常拥有房产、昂贵的游艇，或者在豪华餐厅用餐。

7
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:46,790
And there appear to be more and more of these people, as it‘s reported that the number of super- rich is expected to increase by 43% over the next decade.
而且这类人似乎越来越多，有报道称，未来十年超级富豪的数量预计将增加43%。

8
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:53,070
If you save your pennies, make the right investments and work hard, could you be one of them?
如果你省吃俭用、正确地投资并努力工作，能成为他们中的一员吗？

9
00:00:53,070 --> 00:01:03,320
It’s unlikely because a report last year highlighted inequality in the world, saying the richest 62 individuals owned as much as the poorest 50%.
可能性不大，因为去年一份报告强调了全球的不平等现象，称最富有的62个人拥有的财富相当于最贫穷的50%人口的总和。

10
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:09,340
But for those lucky ones who are loaded, what is it that they splash the cash on?
但对于那些幸运的富豪来说，他们会把钱花在什么上面呢？

11
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:17,480
One academic in the UK, Emma Spence, has been researching just that - and her answer is yachts!
英国学者艾玛·斯彭斯一直在研究这个问题——她的答案是游艇！

12
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:31,370
It‘s the ultimate status symbol but she also says “a superyacht is essentially a black hole of wealth” - in other words, it continually eats your money and doesn’t increase in value like an art collection might.
游艇是终极身份象征，但她也表示“超级游艇本质上是财富黑洞”，换句话说，它会持续消耗你的钱，而且不会像艺术品收藏那样升值。

13
00:01:31,370 --> 00:01:36,580
But if you‘ve got the spare cash, why not have one!
但如果你有闲钱，为什么不买一艘呢？

14
00:01:36,580 --> 00:01:39,300
It’s an excuse to show off your wealth and position in society.
这是一个炫耀财富和社会地位的理由。

15
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:46,010
Interestingly, Emma Spence found that the size of someone‘s yacht shows their place in the pecking order.
有趣的是，艾玛·斯彭斯发现，游艇的大小能体现一个人在等级体系中的地位。

16
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:53,000
This is a good example of conspicuous consumption - buying something so someone else notices.
这是“炫耀性消费”的典型例子——购买某样东西就是为了让别人注意到。

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:06,510
In the past you may have expected to find a super- rich, yacht- owning, billionaire to live in developed countries like the USA but now the wealthy can be found hanging out in most corners of the world.
过去，你可能会认为拥有游艇、超级富有的亿万富翁会住在像美国这样的发达国家，但现在在世界大多数角落都能看到富豪的身影。

18
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:18,670
According to a report by Knight Frank, Vietnam is the country expected to have the fastest growth of super- rich over the next 10 years - an amazing 170% increase.
根据莱坊房地产咨询公司的一份报告，越南是未来10年超级富豪数量增长最快的国家——增幅惊人，达170%。

19
00:02:18,670 --> 00:02:25,070
If all this makes you feel poor, remember that being wealthy doesn‘t necessarily make you happy.
如果这些让你觉得自己贫穷，记住，富有不一定能让你快乐。

20
00:02:25,070 --> 00:02:28,760
You don’t have to waste time worrying about what to spend your money on.
你不必花时间纠结该把钱花在哪里。

21
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:38,220
And you can feel rich in other ways by having good friends and family, good health or just a happy life - things that don‘t cost the earth.
而且你还可以通过拥有亲密的朋友和家人、健康的身体，或者仅仅是幸福的生活来感受“富有”——这些都无需花费巨额财富。

22
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:42,980
And if you really want a yacht, how about a toy one to play with in the bath?!
如果你真的想要一艘游艇，买个能在浴缸里玩的玩具游艇怎么样？

23
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:45,180
How rich do you feel today?
今天的你觉得自己有多“富有”呢？
